a compact grid of turnaround views, 3 columns by 2 rows — front view, left side, three-quarter view, right side, back view, in that order, left-to-right then top-to-bottom — each 341 pixels wide, 480 pixels tall, consistent scale across all cells keep the entire subject inside its own cell with equal empty margin on all four sides, never letting limbs, weapons, or effects cross into a neighbouring cell; render every cell at an identical bounding box and identical pixel scale; cells are separated by background only — no drawn cell borders, dividing lines, gridlines, or gutters; no text, labels, captions, numbers, or watermarks anywhere on the sheet. three facial expression close-ups side by side, left-aligned starting at the left edge — neutral, happy, angry — each 256 pixels wide, 160 pixels tall. a horizontal palette swatch row showing all colours used, 1024 pixels wide, 96 pixels tall. two detail callout panels side by side, each 512 pixels wide, 160 pixels tall. one outfit-variant panel, 256 pixels wide, 160 pixels tall, showing an alternate outfit or colour scheme. White background, consistent scale across all views. Professional sprite sheet format
